Sval: the Troubleshoot Mode dialog names a string that exists

safeMode.xhtml's #resetProfile box, shown after repeated startup crashes,
names refresh-profile-instead, which browser/safeMode.ftl no longer defines,
so Fluent rejects with "Missing message" each time the dialog translates and
the box would show no text. The text it means is the one the dialog's
#resetProfileInstead label already uses, skip-troubleshoot-refresh-profile.
The id is in the dialog's markup, so no chrome API reaches it.

diff --git a/browser/base/content/safeMode.xhtml b/browser/base/content/safeMode.xhtml
index 7b452d2f19..88820a8761 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/safeMode.xhtml
+++ b/browser/base/content/safeMode.xhtml
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
     </vbox>
 
     <vbox id="resetProfile" hidden="true">
-      <label data-l10n-id="refresh-profile-instead" />
+      <label data-l10n-id="skip-troubleshoot-refresh-profile" />
     </vbox>
 
     <separator class="thin" />
